# Security-sensitive paths require security-owner review (GOVERNANCE.md §Reviews).
# A security-owners team replaces the individual owner once the project moves to an organisation
# and a second security owner exists. Last matching pattern wins.

# Every Ring 0 crate, present and future (identity, egress, runtime, api, the bin), and the
# dev-only harnesses whose results gate merges.
/crates/                  @istisnaikal

# Contracts, architecture and the gates that enforce them.
/schemas/                 @istisnaikal
/arch.toml                @istisnaikal
/clippy.toml              @istisnaikal
/deny.toml                @istisnaikal
/gates.toml               @istisnaikal
/xtask/                   @istisnaikal

# Build inputs: a change here changes what every crate compiles against.
